# Line endings (wii-homebrew-kit): text is LF in the repository and in every checkout, on
# every platform, whatever core.autocrlf says. Merge a branch from before this rule (2026-10-24)
# with `git merge -X renormalize`; fix an old checkout with `python tools/fix_line_endings.py`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files: CRLF in the checkout, which cmd.exe needs.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary data.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.bin binary
*.wad binary
*.dol binary
*.elf binary
*.ttf binary
*.wav binary
*.dat binary

# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even on Windows checkouts, or Git Bash
# fails to parse them (CRLF breaks the shebang line and here-docs).
*.sh text eol=lf

# Patches applied by scripts/build.sh: CRLF in a Windows checkout makes `patch` reject them
# (libwupc-libogc3.patch failed in every fresh worktree, 2026-10-18).
*.patch text eol=lf

# The CA bundle is pinned by its SHA-256 (cacert.pem.source). It is LF, like every text file, so
# eol=lf keeps it byte for byte; it was -text while autocrlf could still convert it.
